  "fixture_kind": "public_exact-list_card_data",
  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "Although Doctor's companion is a new variant of the partner ability, the rules for partner have not otherwise changed. Notably, Time Lord Doctors and cards with Doctor's companion do not interact with cards which have another partner ability.",
      "oracle_id": "0d6e76aa-2966-48b7-be4e-2d3e2cc94fc1",
      "published_at": "2023-10-13",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An effect that checks whether you control your commander is satisfied if you control one or both of your two commanders.",
      "oracle_id": "0d6e76aa-2966-48b7-be4e-2d3e2cc94fc1",
      "published_at": "2023-10-13",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Both commanders start in the command zone, and the remaining 98 cards (or 58 cards in a Commander Draft game) of your deck are shuffled to become your library.",
      "oracle_id": "0d6e76aa-2966-48b7-be4e-2d3e2cc94fc1",
      "published_at": "2023-10-13",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Donna's ability triggers when either creature is dealt damage even if one or both were dealt lethal damage.",
      "oracle_id": "0d6e76aa-2966-48b7-be4e-2d3e2cc94fc1",
      "published_at": "2023-10-13",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If Donna is paired with another creature and they are both dealt damage at the same time, the second ability triggers twice.",
      "oracle_id": "0d6e76aa-2966-48b7-be4e-2d3e2cc94fc1",
      "published_at": "2023-10-13",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If something refers to your commander while you have two commanders, it refers to one of them of your choice. If you are instructed to perform an action on your commander (e.g. put it from the command zone into your hand due to Command Beacon), you choose one of your commanders at the time the effect happens.",
      "oracle_id": "0d6e76aa-2966-48b7-be4e-2d3e2cc94fc1",
      "published_at": "2023-10-13",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If your Commander deck has two commanders, you can include only cards whose own color identities are also found in your commanders' combined color identities.",
      "oracle_id": "0d6e76aa-2966-48b7-be4e-2d3e2cc94fc1",
      "published_at": "2023-10-13",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once the game begins, your two commanders are tracked separately. If you cast one, you won't have to pay an additional {2} the first time you cast the other. A player loses the game after having been dealt 21 combat damage from any one of them, not from both of them combined.",
      "oracle_id": "0d6e76aa-2966-48b7-be4e-2d3e2cc94fc1",
      "published_at": "2023-10-13",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The Doctor's companion ability allows you to have two commanders if one has the ability and the other is a legendary creature that is a Time Lord Doctor and has no other creature types. Creatures with the changeling ability, for example, can't be a second commander this way.",
      "oracle_id": "0d6e76aa-2966-48b7-be4e-2d3e2cc94fc1",
      "published_at": "2023-10-13",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If Tandem Lookout or the creature it’s paired with is dealt lethal damage at the same time that either deals damage to an opponent, its ability triggers. You’ll draw a card even though that creature no longer has the ability.",
      "oracle_id": "1576f031-57ca-4894-b461-8ea57b6cefdc",
      "published_at": "2017-03-14",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Use the creature's power as it last existed on the battlefield to determine how many cards to draw.",
      "oracle_id": "172b94a0-2801-4623-aed8-902591c2d591",
      "published_at": "2021-11-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If Druid’s Familiar becomes unpaired, it will immediately lose the +2/+2 bonus. If this causes it to have damage marked on it equal to it or greater than its new toughness, it will be destroyed. The same is true for the creature it was paired with.",
      "oracle_id": "6a5b1cd4-e597-4122-8fc7-4dce241d7c01",
      "published_at": "2012-05-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A creature that loses haste after it’s been declared as an attacking creature doesn’t stop attacking.",
      "oracle_id": "6c5664b1-fbb5-477e-80fd-cf2285014a10",
      "published_at": "2012-05-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you activate the ability granted by Deadeye Navigator, the creature will be exiled, the pair will immediately be broken, and then the card will be returned to the battlefield. Deadeye Navigator’s soulbond ability triggers when that card enters the battlefield and the pair can then be reunited.",
      "oracle_id": "ebef6d84-b724-4a84-bcde-8eb6dc06717d",
      "published_at": "2017-03-14",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once Deadeye Navigator or the creature it’s paired with is exiled, the other creature will no longer have the activated ability. However, you can activate the ability of one creature in response to activating the ability of the other creature.",
      "oracle_id": "ebef6d84-b724-4a84-bcde-8eb6dc06717d",
      "published_at": "2017-03-14",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Diregraf Escort can be paired with a Zombie. The protection will have no effect on the pairing.",
      "oracle_id": "f28a67d8-05ec-4d72-aa17-670ce1136f5c",
      "published_at": "2012-05-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
